# The fusions that owe no exact sum. One row per suspended fusion per quantity, and never more than
# one however many grounds a composer filed.
#
# A suspension is a set, its reasons a bag
#   A suspension is a set and its reasons are a bag, and keeping them in one relation puts a bag
#   where every caller wants a set. `composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc` is the bag: one row per
#   ground, carrying `suspended_because` for anybody who needs to say why. This is the projection
#   onto the key that matters, and it is what an anti-join or a count should read.
#
# The `DISTINCT` is load-bearing
#   It is load-bearing rather than defensive. `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files an
#   unsearched elimination and an unsized conversion, so it appears twice upstream and is suspended
#   once. Dropping the projection inflates every count of suspended fusions by one row per extra
#   ground.
-- composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc projected onto the fusion it suspends.
SELECT DISTINCT g.composition, g.composed_layer, g.quantity
FROM (
    :compose(composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc)
) g
